  <prompt>
    Remove OpenAI AutoRecompose (not needed), and make H0's OpenAI quota and model-version checks test exactly the deployments
    customer.bicep creates, in the region it creates them.
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer (L2 control plane, Azure ARM SDK, Bicep). Follow the provisioning constraints and ADR-038.</role>

  <goal>
    No AutoRecompose code, option, DI registration or test remains. One C# catalog (PinnedModelCatalog) lists the stamp's
    OpenAI deployments (name, model, version, capacity) and the default OpenAI region, and a test fails if it differs from
    the compiled customer.json. H0's TPM-headroom probe requests each model's summed deployment capacity, and both OpenAI
    probes query the run's openAiLocation (else the template default), so a subscription without quota fails at H0.
  </goal>

  <justification>
    <existing>AutoRecompose: BicepInfraDeployOptions.OpenAiDeploymentSetPolicy, IOpenAiDeploymentSetRecomposer, ArmOpenAiDeploymentSetRecomposer, H2a step 8.5, Worker registration — computes a drop set and only logs it (G27). H0: ArmCognitiveServicesTpmProbe (own hard-coded model/TPM table) and ArmOpenAiPinFreshnessProbe (PinnedModelCatalog), both on intake `region`.</existing>
    <extension>Extend PinnedModelCatalog with the deployment rows + default OpenAI region; the probes read it. No new component.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>H0 checks westus2 while OpenAI deploys to westus3, requests text-embedding-3-small (not deployed) and checks gpt-4o 2024-08-06 (deployed: 2024-11-20) — a quota-less subscription passes H0 and fails ~20 minutes into H2a. AutoRecompose, if ever switched on, could only drop a deployment the BFF calls by name (gpt-4o, gpt-4o-mini, text-embedding-3-large), producing a stamp that deploys green and fails at runtime.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <context>
